## User question:
When setting up BGP Monitoring Protocol on our Nokia 7750 SRs, we need to adjust the session establishment parameters — specifically, what would be the recommended approach to modify the connection retry interval to accommodate longer convergence times during maintenance windows, increasing it from the default to a 5-minute threshold?
---
## Proposed answer:
To modify the BGP connection retry interval to 5 minutes (300 seconds) on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp connect-retry 300
```

This command adjusts the BGP connect retry timer globally. For group or neighbor-specific adjustments, navigate to the respective configuration level:

- **Group-level adjustment**:  
  ```
  configure router bgp group <group-name> connect-retry 300
  ```

- **Neighbor-level adjustment**:  
  ```
  configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> connect-retry 300
---
