## User question:
During a routine maintenance window to enhance BGP session visibility, we need to annotate the existing BGP peering group configuration on our Nokia 7750 SR NOS routers with a human-readable identifier that clearly indicates its role in connecting to AS 64500 through the primary transit link—could you advise on implementing this operational metadata using the "BGP_Group_A_Peering" designation?
---
## Proposed answer:
To annotate the BGP peering group with the specified human-readable identifier, apply the following configuration command:

```
/configure router bgp group "BGP_Group_A_Peering" description "Primary transit link to AS 64500"
```

This command adds the description directly to the BGP group configuration, clearly indicating its role for operational visibility.
