Your answer:

To ensure seamless BGP session preservation during NOTIFICATION message exchanges and handle unplanned interruptions without route flaps, configure BGP graceful restart with notification support at the group level:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        graceful-restart
            enable-notification
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**  
- `graceful-restart` enables BGP helper functionality for session recovery.  
- `enable-notification` allows graceful session restart during NOTIFICATION exchanges, preserving forwarding state.  
- The default restart-time (300 seconds) is used unless explicitly modified with `restart-time <seconds>`.  

Apply this configuration to all relevant BGP groups participating in the maintenance.
