To disable capability negotiation for a specific legacy BGP neighbor and enforce strict IPv4-only routing, apply the following configuration at the neighbor level:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-IP>
            disable-capability-negotiation
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**  
- Replace `<group-name>` with the BGP group containing the legacy peer.  
- Replace `<neighbor-IP>` with the IP address of the legacy BGP neighbor.  
- This command prevents the negotiation of extended capabilities (e.g., IPv6, 4-byte ASN) and restricts the session to IPv4 routing exchanges only.  
- Capability negotiation remains disabled until explicitly re-enabled with `no disable-capability-negotiation` when dual-stack migration occurs.  

**Operational note:**  
After applying this configuration, manually reset the BGP session (e.g., `clear router bgp neighbor <neighbor-IP>`) to enforce the change immediately.
------------
