To address the issue of unexpected router IDs in the BGP aggregator attribute during route summarization, configure the `aggregator-id-zero` command at the BGP level. This ensures the router ID in the aggregator path attribute is set to zero for all aggregated routes:

```cli
configure router bgp
    aggregator-id-zero
exit
```

This configuration applies globally to all BGP operations, maintaining consistent and clean path information across multi-vendor domains by eliminating variable router IDs in the aggregator attribute.
