## User question:
During our multicast infrastructure upgrade, we're running into situations where BGP isn't selecting optimal paths for IPv6 multicast traffic due to AS-path length considerations on our Nokia 7750 SR routers. What's the proper way to adjust the best path selection algorithm so it disregards AS-path length specifically for IPv6 multicast RIB entries, while maintaining all other standard BGP decision criteria? We need this change to ensure proper anycast RP functionality across our dual-stack backbone.
---
## Proposed answer:
To adjust the BGP best path selection algorithm to disregard AS-path length specifically for IPv6 multicast RIB entries, use the following configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        as-path-ignore mcast-ipv6
```

This command disables AS-path length comparison for IPv6 multicast routes while preserving all other standard BGP decision criteria, ensuring optimal path selection for anycast RP functionality in your dual-stack backbone.
