To ensure routers properly signal extended LLGR stale-time persistence for a 24-hour duration (86400 seconds), configure the following:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    long-lived
        advertised-stale-time 86400
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
This enables long-lived graceful restart (LLGR) globally under BGP and sets the advertised stale-time to 86400 seconds. Peers will retain stale routes for 24 hours during control-plane outages, preventing premature route flushing. Apply this configuration consistently across all routers in your fleet during the maintenance window.
