To extend the advertised long-lived stale route timer to one hour (3600 seconds) for BGP graceful restart, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            advertised-stale-time 3600
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This command sets the advertised LLGR stale time to 3600 seconds globally under the BGP graceful restart hierarchy.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
When configuring BGP graceful restart capabilities on our Nokia 7750 SR routers to minimize route reconvergence disruptions, we need to ensure that stale routes remain available during neighbor recovery—what’s the appropriate CLI syntax to extend the advertised long-lived stale route timer to one hour (3600 seconds) under the relevant BGP or GR configuration hierarchy?
---
## Proposed answer:
To extend the advertised long-lived stale route timer to one hour (3600 seconds) for BGP graceful restart, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        long-lived
            advertised-stale-time 3600
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This command sets the advertised LLGR stale time to 3600 seconds globally under the BGP graceful restart hierarchy.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
advertised-stale-time <seconds>
no advertised-stale-time
FuncDef:
This command sets the value of the long-lived stale time that is advertised by the router in its LLGR capability. When configured in the long-lived configuration context,advertised-stale-timeapplies to all AFI/SAFI in the advertised LLGR capability except for any AFI/SAFI with a family-specific override. A family-specific override is configured with theadvertised-stale-timecommand in afamilycontext.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'seconds', 'Info': 'Specifies the advertised long-lived stale time in seconds. Values-0 to 16777215.'}
---
