During a recent multicast VPN deployment using IPv6, we encountered a situation where BGP path selection was unnecessarily influenced by router ID comparisons between redundant PE devices. What’s the proper method to adjust the route selection criteria on Huawei NE40E platforms to prioritize other MVPN-specific attributes over the BGP identifier for optimal forwarding?

```console
configure router bgp
    optimal-route-reflection
        location 8
        exit
    exit
    group <edge-group-name>
        cluster 192.168.10.1 orr-location 8 allow-local-fallback
    exit
```

**Implementation Notes:**
1. Replace `<edge-group-name>` with your actual BGP group name
2. The `allow-local-fallback` parameter ensures traffic forwarding continuity by advertising the best locally reachable route when ORR-optimized paths are unavailable
3. The `orr-location 8` binding ensures path optimization for clients in this cluster
4. Location ID 8 must be pre-configured under `optimal-route-reflection` before group configuration

**Verification Commands:**
```console
show router bgp group <edge-group-name> detail | match "Cluster|ORR"
show router bgp orr location
```
