To ensure your Nokia 7750 SR properly handles IPv4 routes with the link-bandwidth extended community from external BGP peers, use the following CLI configuration. Apply this under the relevant BGP group or neighbor context for your EBGP peers:

```cli
configure
router
    bgp
        group <ebgp_group_name>
            link-bandwidth
                accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            exit
```

**Key details:**
- Replace `<ebgp_group_name>` with your EBGP peer group name.
- This configuration accepts and processes the link-bandwidth attribute for IPv4 routes received from all EBGP peers in the specified group.
- No additional policy modifications are required to accept the attribute—this command explicitly enables processing.

For neighbor-specific configuration (if needed):
```cli
configure
router
    bgp
        group <ebgp_group_name>
            neighbor <ip_address>
                link-bandwidth
                    accept-from-ebgp ipv4
                exit
```
