To ensure seamless BGP session recovery with explicit signaling for NOTIFICATION message compatibility during your core router upgrade, configure the following:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        graceful-restart
            enable-notification
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**
- `graceful-restart` enables BGP graceful restart procedures at the router level.
- `enable-notification` explicitly signals that your router supports session preservation when NOTIFICATION messages are exchanged during reestablishment.
- Restart-time defaults to 120 seconds at this configuration level, which is typically sufficient for maintenance operations.

This configuration ensures peers recognize your router's graceful restart capabilities during session reestablishment, including compatibility with NOTIFICATION-based restarts. Apply this globally under BGP configuration to cover all peers supporting this feature.
