To address the intermittent BGP peering session flaps by extending the Connect Retry timer to 90 seconds, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    connect-retry 90
```

This command sets the BGP Connect Retry timer to 90 seconds globally for all peers. If the adjustment is needed for a specific peer group or neighbor, apply the command under the relevant context. For example, for a group named "WAN_Peers":

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "WAN_Peers"
        connect-retry 90
```

Or for a specific neighbor (e.g., IP address 192.0.2.1) within that group:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "WAN_Peers"
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            connect-retry 90
``` 

The value `90` must be within the valid range (1-65535 seconds) and replaces the default 120-second timer. Adjust the scope (global, group, or neighbor) based on your specific peer stability requirements.
