"During a recent maintenance window, we observed excessive route churn causing instability in our BGP peering sessions with a Huawei NE40E router. To mitigate this, I need to implement a rate-limiting mechanism that enforces a 60-second cooldown period between consecutive prefix advertisements, ensuring more stable routing updates without impacting legitimate convergence events."

To implement enhanced BGP error handling for improved fault tolerance without disrupting existing peer sessions, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure
    router "Base"
        bgp
            error-handling
                update-fault-tolerance
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This sequence enables non-disruptive handling of UPDATE message errors by treating them as withdrawals while avoiding session resets. Apply these commands during your maintenance window.
