To enforce a local LLGR stale time of one hour (3600 seconds) and override peer-advertised values, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    purge-timer 60
    graceful-restart
        stale-routes-time 3600
        long-lived
            helper-override-stale-time 3600
            advertised-stale-time 3600
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `purge-timer 60` sets the maximum time for stale route retention to 60 minutes (1 hour), aligning with the desired LLGR duration.  
- `stale-routes-time 3600` ensures BGP maintains stale routes for 3600 seconds (1 hour) during graceful restart.  
- `helper-override-stale-time 3600` overrides any LLGR stale-time values received from peers with the local 1-hour setting.  
- `advertised-stale-time 3600` advertises a consistent 1-hour stale-time to peers, promoting domain-wide stability.  

This configuration globally enforces the 1-hour LLGR policy while overriding conflicting peer values.
