During a multicast VPN deployment on our Huawei NE40E routers, we need to ensure optimal path diversity while maintaining control over route propagation—what’s the recommended way to limit outbound advertisements to 8 distinct paths per IPv4 prefix for multicast routes while also preventing the acceptance of multiple paths from BGP peers to avoid unnecessary route churn?

To ensure route integrity by confirming the autonomous system at the end of each incoming path matches your established neighbor configurations, apply the following command at the relevant BGP group or neighbor level:

```console
configure router bgp
    group "EBGP_GROUP"
        enforce-first-as
    exit
exit
```

