During a recent core router upgrade, we noticed persistent IP fragmentation issues during high-throughput transfers across our Huawei NE40E-based MPLS backbone. What’s the recommended way to configure TCP path MTU discovery dynamically via ICMP feedback on these platforms, ensuring sessions adapt without manual intervention while avoiding fragmentation penalties?

```
configure
    bmp
        station <station-name>
            connection
                tcp-keepalive
                    keep-interval 30
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Important Notes:**  
1. Replace `<station-name>` with the actual BMP station name configured on your router  
2. This sets the TCP keepalive probe interval to 30 seconds for the specified BMP station  
3. The first keepalive probe will still follow the default `keep-idle` timer (600 seconds) unless separately modified  

To verify the configuration:  
```
show bmp station <station-name> detail
```
