Based on your request to configure the TCP keepalive probe retransmission interval to 30 seconds, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure
bmp
    station <station-name>
        connection
            tcp-keepalive
                keep-interval 30
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key details:**  
- `keep-interval` controls the time between TCP keepalive probes when no response is received  
- The value `30` sets the retransmission timer to 30 seconds (valid range: 1-100000 seconds)  
- This configuration applies to BMP station connections where TCP session stability is managed  

Replace `<station-name>` with your specific BMP station identifier. The default interval of 15 seconds is now extended to reduce control plane load while maintaining session persistence.
