During a recent core router upgrade project, we're encountering path MTU discovery issues where TCP sessions aren't properly adjusting packet sizes despite receiving ICMP fragmentation-needed messages—what's the recommended method to configure our Huawei NE40E platforms to dynamically adapt MSS values based on ICMP feedback to optimize throughput without manual intervention?

To adjust the route selection criteria for MVPN IPv6 on Nokia 7750 SR platforms and prioritize MVPN-specific attributes over the router ID, configure the following:

```console
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ignore-router-id include-internal mvpn-ipv6
    exit
exit
```

This configuration modifies the BGP best-path algorithm to skip router ID comparisons for MVPN IPv6 routes, allowing other MVPN-specific attributes to determine the optimal path.
