To enforce "core-link-1" as the source interface for all BGP sessions in the backbone traffic peer group, apply the following configuration:

```console
configure router bgp
    group "backbone-group"
        local-address "core-link-1"
    exit
exit
```

**Key points:**  
- This configuration sets `core-link-1` as the source interface for **all peers** in the specified group (`backbone-group`).  
- Replace `backbone-group` with your actual peer group name handling backbone traffic.  
- Ensures no fallback to loopback/other interfaces by overriding any inherited settings.  

> ⚠️ **Verification Step**: After applying, verify with `show router bgp group "backbone-group" detail` to confirm `Local Address` reflects `core-link-1`.
------------
