During our recent network upgrade where we're implementing BGP Monitoring Protocol across all core routers, I need to configure our Huawei NE40E platforms to advertise locally originated routes to the BMP collector—could you walk me through the specific steps required to establish this reporting functionality without disrupting existing BGP sessions?

To achieve seamless route propagation between routing instances with the specified requirements, apply the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    rib-management
        ipv4
            leak-import "CUST_A_POLICY"
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration uses the `leak-import` command under the base router's BGP IPv4 RIB management to selectively import leak-eligible routes from peer VRFs. The `CUST_A_POLICY` (which must be pre-configured in `policy-options` to enforce the compound condition `POLICY_B AND POLICY_C`) controls route selection. Only routes matching this policy will be imported into the default instance's unlabeled IPv4 forwarding table, maintaining route segregation boundaries.
