To ensure proper next-hop resolution for unimported VPN-IPv4 and VPN-IPv6 routes on the Nokia 7750 SR, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    enable-rr-vpn-forwarding
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family vpn
                    resolution-filter
                        ldp
                        rsvp
                        sr-isis
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

### Key actions:
1. **`enable-rr-vpn-forwarding`**  
   Imports all VPN routes into a dummy VRF for next-hop resolution, enabling proper forwarding without binding to specific VPRN instances.

2. **`family vpn` under transport-tunnel**  
   Configures next-hop resolution exclusively for unimported VPN-IPv4/VPN-IPv6 routes.

3. **`resolution-filter`**  
   Specifies acceptable tunnel types (LDP, RSVP, SR-ISIS) for resolving BGP next-hops. Adjust these based on your network's available tunnels.

> **Note**:  
> - Replace `ldp`, `rsvp`, and `sr-isis` with your actual tunnel types.  
> - Avoid `sr-policy` in the filter—VPN routes don't support SR-policy resolution.  
> - This configuration maintains route isolation while ensuring unresolved routes get forwarded.
------------
