```console
configure router
    bgp
        ibgp-multipath
        best-path-selection
            ignore-router-id
            ebgp-ibgp-equal ipv4 ipv6
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables iBGP multipath load balancing (`ibgp-multipath`) to allow multiple iBGP paths to be installed in the routing table
2. Activates router ID ignoring in best-path selection (`ignore-router-id`) to treat paths with identical attributes as equal regardless of router IDs
3. Enables EIBGP path equivalence (`ebgp-ibgp-equal`) for IPv4/IPv6 to allow load balancing across both eBGP and iBGP paths

These commands work together to maximize path utilization for equal-cost BGP paths while maintaining normal route advertisement behavior.
