- This configuration is applied under the BGP `graceful-restart > long-lived` hierarchy, ensuring the F-bit is disabled *only* for the specified control-plane families.  
- All other AFI/SAFI pairs retain their default F-bit behavior (F-bit set to `0`), preserving normal forwarding operations.  

