"During a core network upgrade where we're migrating from RSVP-TE tunnels to segment routing, I need to ensure BGP-labeled routes on our Huawei NE40E routers resolve next-hops via the IGP routing table rather than relying on legacy tunnel protocol lookups—what's the proper configuration approach to enforce this behavior?"

To resolve the path MTU discovery issues and enable dynamic MSS adaptation for TCP sessions on your Nokia 7750 SR, enable path MTU discovery in the BGP configuration context:

```
configure router bgp
    path-mtu-discovery
```

This configuration ensures BGP TCP sessions:
1. Initially set the MTU to the egress interface's MTU
2. Enable the DF (Don't Fragment) bit in packets
3. Dynamically adjust the path MTU based on received ICMP fragmentation-needed messages
4. Optimize throughput without requiring manual MSS adjustments

The change applies to all BGP peers globally. For granular control, you can optionally configure it under specific BGP groups or neighbors using the same command in those sub-contexts.
