To ensure all address families from a BGP peer adhere to a customized recovery timer of 300 seconds during Graceful Restart, configure the following commands at the neighbor level:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <peer-ip>
            graceful-restart
                stale-routes-time 300
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `graceful-restart` enables helper functionality for all negotiated address families.  
- `stale-routes-time 300` overrides any peer-advertised restart timers, maintaining stale routes for 300 seconds after a peer restart.  

Replace `<group-name>` and `<peer-ip>` with your specific BGP group and neighbor IP address. This configuration ensures the router preserves routes for the full 300-second recovery window, regardless of default or peer-negotiated values.
