## Proposed answer:
To enable entropy labels for BGP-based tunneling without disrupting existing labeled unicast routes, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    override-tunnel-elc
    exit
```

This configuration enables entropy label capability (ELC) on BGP tunnels to improve load-balancing efficiency. The command operates globally under BGP settings and does not affect existing labeled unicast routes.
