This command configures the add-paths capability for unlabeled IPv4 unicast routes. By default, add-paths is not enabled for unlabeled IPv4 unicast routes.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'send-limit', 'Info': 'Specifies the maximum number of paths per unlabeled IPv4 unicast prefix that are allowed to be advertised to add-paths peers. (The actual number of advertised routes may be less.) If the value is none, the router does not negotiate the send capability with respect to IPv4 AFI/SAFI. Values-1 to 16, none.'}
{'Parameters': 'receive', 'Info': 'Specifies that the router negotiates to receive multiple unlabeled unicast routes per IPv4 prefix.'}
{'Parameters': 'none', 'Info': 'Specifies that the router does not negotiate to receive multiple unlabeled unicast routes per IPv4 prefix.'}
