To configure long-lived graceful restart for BGP peers during maintenance, use the following CLI commands on your Nokia 7750 SR routers. Adjust the `group "CorePeers"` name and timer values as needed:

```cli
configure router bgp
   group "CorePeers"
      graceful-restart
         restart-time 300
         long-lived
            stale-routes-time 3600
         exit
         enable-notification
      exit
   exit
exit
```

**Key parameters explained:**  
- `graceful-restart`: Enables BGP helper functionality for all negotiated address families.  
- `restart-time 300`: Sets the standard GR restart duration (default: 300 seconds).  
- `long-lived`: Activates long-lived GR extensions.  
- `stale-routes-time 3600`: Preserves stale routes for up to 1 hour during extended outages.  
- `enable-notification`: Allows session persistence during NOTIFICATION events.  

Apply this configuration to all BGP groups/neighbors requiring uninterrupted routing during reboots. Ensure consistent GR capabilities across all peers.
