To address the issue of BGP-labeled IPv4 routes not resolving /32 loopbacks via LDP, configure LDP tunneling for next-hop reachability in the BGP labeled-routes context. Use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter ldp
```

### Key points:
1. **`family ipv4`**: Specifies IPv4 route resolution (required for /32 loopbacks).
2. **`resolution-filter ldp`**: Explicitly enables LDP tunneling for next-hop resolution of labeled IPv4 routes.

This configuration ensures BGP uses LDP FECs to resolve /32 next-hop reachability for labeled unicast routes. If other tunnel types (e.g., RSVP, SR) are needed alongside LDP, include them in the same `resolution-filter` command (e.g., `resolution-filter ldp rsvp`).
