## User question:
During a recent core network upgrade, we're implementing BGP route reflectors to optimize iBGP scaling across our Nokia 7750 SR router fleet. Could you walk me through assigning 192.168.100.1 as the primary loopback interface address that will serve as the stable endpoint for all route reflector client sessions? I need to ensure this configuration maintains optimal path reflection while meeting our addressing scheme requirements.
---
## Proposed answer:
To assign 192.168.100.1 as the primary loopback interface address for the route reflector and ensure optimal path reflection, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        optimal-route-reflection
            location 1 primary-ip-address 192.168.100.1
---
