To transition a specific BGP peer from passive to active mode while keeping others unaffected and ensuring immediate adjacency establishment, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            no passive
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the BGP group containing the peer and `<neighbor-ip>` with the peer's IP address. This disables passive mode for the specified neighbor, allowing your router to initiate the BGP session immediately without impacting other peers.
------------
