2. `extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4` enables the router to accept/propagate IPv6 next hops for labeled IPv4 routes, maintaining dual-stack consistency.  
3. `rr-use-route-table` forces the route reflector to use the IGP route table (instead of tunnel table) for next-hop resolution of labeled routes, preventing recursive lookups and compatibility issues in multi-vendor environments.  

Apply this configuration to the BGP group containing your route-reflector clients. Ensure all peers support RFC 8950 extended next-hop encoding.
