To implement an automatic purge mechanism for outdated BGP VPN-IP routes with a 15-minute timeout, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    purge-timer 15
```

This command sets the maximum time for stale VPN-IP routes to be retained in the RIB-IN to 15 minutes. Routes that fail to refresh within this period are automatically purged, preventing routing table bloat while maintaining service continuity. The configuration operates at the global BGP level and applies to all VPN-IP routes received from peers.
