To configure the router ID for BGP peering on your Nokia 7750 SR platform, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    router-id 192.0.2.1
```

This sets the system-wide router ID to `192.0.2.1` in dotted decimal format, which BGP will inherit by default. If you require a BGP-specific override (e.g., to use a different ID than the system router ID), enter the BGP context and set it explicitly:

```
configure router bgp
    router-id 192.0.2.1
```
