To ensure the link-bandwidth attribute is properly attached to IPv4 routes when sharing with external BGP neighbors without label distribution, configure the following:

```
configure router bgp
    group <external_group_name>
        link-bandwidth
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
        exit
    exit
```

**Key details:**
- The `link-bandwidth` command enables capacity signaling under the BGP group or neighbor context.
- `aggregate-used-paths ipv4` attaches the link-bandwidth extended community to unlabeled IPv4 routes by aggregating bandwidth values from multipaths when advertising routes with `next-hop-self`.
- This configuration applies to EBGP peers within the specified group to propagate bandwidth information across autonomous systems.
