To address BGP route withdrawal delays and prevent persistent blackholing on your Nokia 7750 SR routers, implement the following configuration adjustments:

```cli
configure router bgp
    rapid-withdrawal
    enable-peer-tracking
    hold-time 30 min 30
exit
```

### Key changes explained:
1. **rapid-withdrawal**  
   Disables the default delay in sending BGP withdrawals, ensuring immediate propagation during topology changes.

2. **enable-peer-tracking**  
   Accelerates BGP session teardown when the route to a peer becomes unreachable, bypassing hold-time expiration.

3. **hold-time 30 min 30**  
   Sets the session hold-time to 30 seconds (with a minimum acceptable value of 30 seconds) for faster failure detection while maintaining negotiated stability with peers.

> **Implementation Notes**  
> - Coordinate `hold-time` adjustments with peering partners to ensure session compatibility.  
> - Validate changes in a maintenance window and monitor session stability post-implementation.  
> - The `purge-timer` (default 10 minutes) was not adjusted as it governs stale VPN-IP route cleanup, not core withdrawal propagation.
