To temporarily isolate a BGP peer while preserving its session parameters on a Nokia 7750 SR, use the `shutdown` command under the specific neighbor configuration. This administratively disables the session without altering any configuration settings:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            neighbor <peer-ip-address>
                shutdown
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the BGP group name and `<peer-ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. To restore the session later, re-enable it with `no shutdown`:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            neighbor <peer-ip-address>
                no shutdown
```
