To configure BGP for propagating locally defined SR policies as self-originated routes to external peers, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        sr-policy-import
        group "external-peers"
            family sr-policy-ipv4
        exit
    exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- `sr-policy-import`: Imports static SR policies into BGP, treating them as self-originated routes for advertisement.  
- `family sr-policy-ipv4`: Enables the SR Policy IPv4 address family for the BGP group "external-peers" (replace with your group name), allowing propagation to peers supporting this capability.  

Ensure your SR policies are statically configured, and apply this configuration to all relevant BGP groups or neighbors interacting with SR-capable peers.
