To ensure BGP-labeled IPv4 routes properly resolve their next hops over MPLS transport tunnels, configure BGP next-hop resolution to use the transport tunnel infrastructure explicitly. The following CLI commands enable resolution via BGP tunnels and Segment Routing policies for IPv4-labeled routes:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter bgp
                    resolution-filter sr-policy
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration directs BGP to resolve next hops for IPv4-labeled routes using either:
- **BGP tunnels**: Leverages BGP label-unicast IPv4 routes (/32 prefixes) for next-hop resolution.
- **Segment Routing policies**: Uses statically configured or BGP-learned SR policies (color-extended community matching required).

Both tunnel types are explicitly enabled in the resolution filter to ensure the label stack imposed by the transport infrastructure is correctly accounted for during next-hop resolution.
