To gracefully suspend BGP peering while preserving the neighbor configuration, use the `shutdown` command under the specific neighbor context. This administratively disables the session without deleting any parameters. After maintenance, re-enable it with `no shutdown`.

**CLI Commands:**  
```  
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> shutdown  
```  

**To restore the session after maintenance:**  
```  
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> no shutdown  
```  

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address.
