To set up the BMP monitoring station "NYC-DC1" on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the following CLI configuration commands. Replace `<ip-address>` and `<port>` with the monitoring station's actual IP address and TCP port:

```cli
/configure bmp
    station "NYC-DC1" create
        connection
            station-address <ip-address> port <port>
            no shutdown
        exit
    exit
exit
/configure router bgp
    monitor
        station "NYC-DC1"
        route-monitoring pre-policy post-policy
    exit
exit
```

**Key parameters explained:**  
- `station-address`: Defines the monitoring station's IP and listening port (mandatory).  
- `route-monitoring pre-policy post-policy`: Enables sending both pre-policy (raw) and post-policy (filtered) BGP route updates to the station.  
- `no shutdown`: Activates the BMP station connection.  

**Verification commands:**  
```cli
show bmp station "NYC-DC1" connection
show router bgp monitor
```
