To ensure uninterrupted BGP operation during maintenance when receiving malformed UPDATE messages with parseable NLRI fields, enable the `update-fault-tolerance` feature. This configuration treats errors non-disruptively while preserving valid routes and session stability:

```
configure router bgp
    error-handling
        update-fault-tolerance
    exit
exit
```

This activates `treat-as-withdraw` behavior for UPDATE errors that don't prevent NLRI parsing, maintaining session stability and valid routes. Apply this globally to affect all peers, or optionally configure under specific groups/neighbors using the same hierarchy.
