To ensure BGP next-hop resolution prioritizes the least preferred IS-IS instances' SR tunnels, configure the following:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunn
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter
                    sr-isis
                exit
            exit
            family ipv6
                resolution-filter
                    sr-isis
                exit
            exit
        exit
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        sr-isis
                    exit
                exit
                family ipv6
                    resolution-filter
                        sr-isis
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables BGP to resolve next hops using SR tunnels from the IS-IS instance with the lowest preference value. If multiple instances share the same preference, the lowest-numbered IS-IS instance is selected. The solution applies to both IPv4 and IPv6 families across standard BGP routes and labeled BGP routes.
------------
