## User question:
"During a core network upgrade where we're migrating from RSVP-TE tunnels to segment routing, I need to ensure BGP-labeled routes on our Nokia 7750 SR routers resolve next-hops via the IGP routing table rather than relying on legacy tunnel protocol lookups—what's the proper configuration approach to enforce this behavior?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To enforce BGP-labeled routes resolving next-hops via the IGP routing table using Segment Routing instead of legacy RSVP-TE tunnels, apply the following configuration:

```cli
/configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family ipv4 resolution-filter
no rsvp
sr-isis
exit
exit
family ipv6 resolution-filter
no rsvp
sr-isis
exit
exit
```

