To implement a secondary loopback interface with IP 192.168.10.20 for BGP optimal route reflection (ORR), use the following CLI sequence:

```bash
configure router
    bgp
        optimal-route-reflection
            location <location-id> secondary-ip-address 192.168.10.20
```

**Key details**:  
- Replace `<location-id>` with your existing ORR location identifier (1-16).  
- This adds the backup loopback IP to the specified location without modifying active peerings.  
- Ensure the loopback interface is pre-configured at the system level.  

**Verification**:  
```bash
show router bgp orr location
```
