To assign 192.0.2.10 as the third IPv4 loopback address for optimizing iBGP next-hop reachability between route reflectors and clients, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp optimal-route-reflection
location <location-id> tertiary-ip-address 192.0.2.10
```

**Replace `<location-id>`** with the appropriate numeric identifier (1–16) for your existing route-reflector location configuration. This adds the tertiary loopback without modifying primary/secondary addresses or disrupting active BGP sessions.  

**Prerequisite:**  
Ensure the loopback interface with 192.0.2.10/32 is pre-configured under `configure router interface` before applying this command.
