To enable BGP next-hop resolution for labeled prefixes over UDP-based tunnels while maintaining existing TCP sessions, use the following configuration sequence:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter udp
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Key actions performed:**
1. Enables UDP tunnel selection under the BGP next-hop resolution hierarchy for IPv4 labeled routes
2. Maintains coexistence with existing TCP-established BGP sessions
3. Allows BGP to resolve labeled prefixes via UDP tunnels without affecting current forwarding consistency
4. Uses the exact context path specified in the reference documentation for UDP tunnel integration (`config>router>bgp>next-hop-resolution>labeled-routes>transport-tunnel>family>resolution-filter`)

This configuration specifically activates UDP tunnel resolution for BGP labeled IPv4 routes while preserving existing transport mechanisms. The order of operations ensures smooth integration during your MPLS core migration.
