To enforce a 15-second threshold between consecutive BGP route advertisements and reduce excessive churn on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the `min-route-advertisement` command. Apply it at the appropriate BGP hierarchy level (global, group, or neighbor) based on your requirements. Here are the CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    min-route-advertisement 15
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
This configures a minimum 15-second interval between successive BGP updates for the same prefix to peers. It stabilizes routing by throttling rapid prefix updates while maintaining convergence, as it only delays redundant advertisements for unstable prefixes. The default value (30 seconds) is lowered to 15 seconds to align with your optimization goal. Apply this command at the `group` or `neighbor` level if specific peers require adjustment.
