```router
configure
    bmp
        station "NYC-DC1" create
            connection
                router Base  # Replace with VPRN name if required
            exit
        exit
        station "LAX-DC2" create
            connection
                router Base  # Replace with VPRN name if required
            exit
        exit
    exit
    router
        bgp
            monitor
                station "NYC-DC1" "LAX-DC2"
                route-monitoring pre-policy post-policy
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key configuration notes:**
1. Both monitoring stations (`NYC-DC1` and `LAX-DC2`) are defined under the global BMP context with their respective routing instances
2. The BGP monitor configuration enables both stations simultaneously
3. Full route visibility is achieved with both pre-policy (raw) and post-policy (processed) route monitoring messages
4. Station names are enclosed in double quotes to handle special characters in the naming convention
5. Replace `router Base` with your specific routing instance (e.g., `router service-name <vprn-name>` if using VPRN transport)

**Verification commands:**
```router
show router bgp monitor
show bmp station detail
```
