To assign 192.168.10.3 as the tertiary IPv4 address for BGP optimal route reflection, use the following CLI configuration sequence. Replace `<id>` with the specific location ID (1-16):

```console
configure router
    bgp
        orr
            location <id>
                tertiary-ip-address 192.168.10.3
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

**Key notes**:  
- This command adds the tertiary IP address to an **existing** location configuration under BGP optimal route reflection.  
- Existing BGP sessions remain stable as this change only modifies the ORR reference addresses.  
- Verify the location ID `<id>` is already configured with primary/secondary addresses per your ORR design.  

If the location doesn't exist yet, first create it with all required addresses:  
```console
location <id> primary-ip-address <primary-ip> secondary-ip-address <secondary-ip> tertiary-ip-address 192.168.10.3
```
