To implement BGP Monitoring Protocol (BMP) for peer session health tracking on your Nokia 7750 SR router without disrupting production traffic, configure route monitoring at the neighbor level. This ensures granular visibility into pre-policy and post-policy routes for specific peers:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            neighbor <peer-ip>
                monitor
                    route-monitoring pre-policy post-policy
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key notes:**
1. Replace `<group-name>` and `<peer-ip>` with your BGP group and neighbor IP
2. `pre-policy` captures incoming routes before local policies apply
3. `post-policy` captures routes after outbound policies are enforced
4. The configuration is applied per-neighbor to minimize impact

For session health tracking, BMP automatically generates peer-up/down notifications when configured this way. To further accelerate failure detection without affecting BMP, consider enabling peer tracking globally:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        enable-peer-tracking
    exit
exit
```
